    {"duration":39.810612,"alignment":{"characters":"In summary, referred pain is visceral pain that is perceived on the body surface. Visceral and somatic nociceptors converge on the same ascending tract in the spinal cord. Because cutaneous pain is more common, the brain attributes the signal to the skin. As for the classic referrals, the heart refers to the chest and left arm, and the liver and gall bladder to the shoulder region. The stomach, small intestine and colon refer to successive bands of the central abdomen. Lastly, the appendix refers to the periumbilical region, and the ureters to the groin. And that's referred pain, a signal from the organs that the brain reads as coming from the skin.","starts":[0,80,160,240,297,354,411,469,526,583,640,960,1040,1080,1120,1173,1227,1280,1333,1387,1440,1640,1690,1740,1790,1840,1920,1960,2000,2160,2213,2267,2320,2440,2470,2500,2530,2560,2720,2760,2800,2840,2880,2920,2930,2940,2950,2960,3040,3080,3120,3200,3253,3307,3360,3413,3467,3520,3573,3627,3680,3760,3800,3840,3920,3947,3973,4000,4120,4150,4180,4210,4240,4320,4469,4617,4766,4914,5063,5211,5360,5440,5520,5547,5573,5600,5720,5750,5780,5810,5840,5920,5947,5973,6000,6040,6080,6147,6213,6280,6347,6413,6480,6560,6613,6667,6720,6827,6933,7040,7080,7120,7173,7227,7280,7360,7413,7467,7520,7600,7680,7760,7800,7840,7920,7960,8000,8080,8107,8133,8160,8240,8300,8360,8420,8480,8720,8747,8773,8800,8827,8853,8880,8907,8933,8960,9120,9152,9184,9216,9248,9280,9360,9400,9440,9480,9493,9507,9520,9600,9680,9760,9820,9880,9940,10000,10360,10450,10540,10630,10720,10827,10933,10949,10964,10979,10994,11010,11025,11040,11120,11200,11280,11360,11413,11467,11520,11573,11627,11680,11760,11800,11840,11880,11920,12000,12040,12080,12200,12230,12260,12290,12320,12640,12693,12747,12800,12853,12907,12960,13000,13040,13067,13093,13120,13280,13312,13344,13376,13408,13440,13680,13704,13728,13752,13776,13800,13824,13848,13872,13896,13920,14000,14027,14053,14080,14280,14313,14347,14380,14413,14447,14480,